course: dictionary
lesson: 13419
title: Hitchhike: a free ride, or a clinging seed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To hitchhike means to travel by standing at the side of the road and asking drivers for a free ride, often by holding up your thumb. The person who does it is a hitchhiker. «Never hitchhike, and never get into a stranger's car, even if they offer you sweets.» This is a safety rule, so a child should always ask a trusted grown-up for help getting home.
explain: Hitchhike has a second meaning. When a small creature or a seed clings to something and travels with it, we say it hitchhikes. «Seeds hitchhike on your socks» means the seeds stick to your socks and get carried to a new place. The seeds do not ask anyone for a ride; they simply cling on.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. If the sentence mentions a road, a driver or a thumb, it is the first meaning. If it mentions seeds, fur or boots, it is the second. Then swap in another phrase, such as "asked for a free ride" or "clung on and travelled", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Hitchhike is a verb: I hitchhike, she hitchhikes, they hitchhiked, we are hitchhiking.
fact: A hitchhiker is the person who hitchhikes.
fact: «Hitchhike» means to ask drivers for a free ride, often by holding up your thumb.
fact: «Hitchhike» can also mean a small creature or seed clings to something to travel, as in «seeds hitchhike on your socks».
fact: Children should never hitchhike or get into a stranger's car; always ask a trusted grown-up for help.
exercise: «The traveller had no money, so he tried to hitchhike across the desert.» What does hitchhike mean here? | To dig a hole in the sand | To swim across a river | *To ask drivers for a free ride | To buy a ticket at the station
exercise: Sam's mum says, «Never hitchhike, and never get into a stranger's car.» What should Sam do if he needs a ride home? | Walk alone along the dark road | Stand at the side of the road and hold up his thumb | Get into the first car that stops | *Ask a trusted grown-up for help
exercise: «Burrs hitchhike on the fur of the dog and fall off far away.» What does hitchhike mean here? | To sing a happy song | To ask a driver for a ride | *To cling to something and travel with it | To run very fast
test: «The seeds hitchhiked on the muddy boots of the walkers.» What does hitchhiked mean in this sentence? | Grew into a tall plant | Were eaten by birds | Fell onto the ground and sank | *Clung on and travelled with the boots
test: What is a hitchhiker? | A driver who gives free rides | A small bird that sings by the road | A tree that grows along roads | *A person who asks drivers for a free ride
exam: Which sentence uses hitchhike to mean clinging and travelling? | The hitchhiker waved at the passing cars. | *Tiny seeds hitchhiked on the bird's feathers across the sea. | Ella held up her thumb to hitchhike to town.
